## Critical: QUpload Syntax Validator Compatibility

This plugin is deployed via QUpload, which validates uploaded PHP files using `token_get_all($content, TOKEN_PARSE)`. Certain valid PHP patterns cause false-positive syntax errors that **block plugin activation**.

### BLOCKED Patterns (Never Use)

| Pattern | Why | Replacement |
|---------|-----|-------------|
| `is_array($var)` | Token `array` causes parse error | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpArray->value` |
| `is_string($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpString->value` |
| `is_int($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpInteger->value` |
| `is_float($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpDouble->value` |
| `is_bool($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpBoolean->value` |
| `is_object($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpObject->value` |
| `is_null($var)` | Same issue | `gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpNull->value` |
| `array()` constructor | T_ARRAY token | Use `[]` short syntax |
| `= array()` default | T_ARRAY token | Use `= []` |
| Magic strings like `=== 'array'` | Not typed | Use `PhpNativeType::PhpArray->value` |

### SAFE Patterns (OK to Use)

| Pattern | Why Safe |
|---------|----------|
| `in_array()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING, not T_ARRAY |
| `array_merge()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING |
| `array_filter()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING |
| `array_map()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING |
| `array_key_exists()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING |
| `array_splice()` | Tokenizes as T_STRING |

### PhpNativeType Enum

Located at `includes/Enums/PhpNativeType.php`:

```php
use RiseupAsia\Enums\PhpNativeType;

// CORRECT
gettype($var) === PhpNativeType::PhpArray->value
gettype($var) !== PhpNativeType::PhpString->value
```

Always add the `use` import when using PhpNativeType.

